1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,270
You have paid this every month for six years.

2
00:00:04,270 --> 00:00:06,630
You have never touched it.

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:09,990
The number is bigger now than the day you walked out.

4
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:13,600
So look at what you actually signed.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:15,580
They handed you a sum.

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:18,640
You agreed to hand back a slice of what you earn —

7
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,500
but only the part above a line.

8
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,290
Earn under the line, you pay nothing.

9
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:27,190
Over it, a percentage.

10
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:31,640
Plan Two. Income-driven. Deferment.

11
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:33,480
Same machine.

12
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:38,360
And most people stop reading right there. Because that does sound fair.

13
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:42,300
It would be. If the number sat still while you paid it.

14
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:43,400
It doesn't.

15
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,720
Every single day, interest is added —

16
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:50,660
not to the part you haven't paid yet, but to the whole outstanding balance.

17
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:53,880
Which means there are two flows here, not one.

18
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:59,340
Money leaving you every month. A slice of your salary, capped by law.

19
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:07,030
And money being added every month. A percentage of everything you owe, uncapped, growing with the balance itself.

20
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:10,180
Now hold those two side by side.

21
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:16,100
Somewhere there is an income where they are exactly equal. Call it the crossover.

22
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:22,050
Earn above it, and your payment eats the interest and starts on the balance. The debt falls.

23
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:31,120
Earn below it, and the balance does not fall slowly. It does not fall at all. It rises. While you pay it.

24
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:37,530
Ten years of payments, never missed, and you owe more than the day you started.

25
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:43,690
That is not what happens when you default. That is what happens when you comply.

26
00:01:43,690 --> 00:01:46,440
And notice which way it cuts.

27
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:51,560
The graduate who earns well crosses over, clears it, and stops paying.

28
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:58,490
The graduate who earns less pays every month for thirty years and never clears anything.

29
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:04,220
Same debt. The one with less money pays longer, and pays more.

30
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:08,030
Then, decades in, the balance is written off.

31
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:13,970
Which sounds like mercy. It isn't. It's the pricing.

32
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:20,130
The lender's own forecasts already assume a large share of borrowers will never clear the balance.

33
00:02:20,130 --> 00:02:27,680
The write-off isn't the escape hatch at the end of the machine. It is a line in the machine's own budget.

34
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:31,930
And this is exactly what the prohibition is pointing at.

35
00:02:31,930 --> 00:02:36,790
Riba isn't a tax on borrowing. It is a price charged for time.

36
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:45,690
A number that grows because the clock moved — not because anything was built, sold, or risked.

37
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:51,400
A debt you service faithfully and cannot reduce is the purest version of that there is.

38
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:54,360
So here is the two-minute check.

39
00:02:54,360 --> 00:03:00,620
One. Find two published numbers: your interest rate, and your repayment threshold.

40
00:03:00,620 --> 00:03:06,470
Two. Work out one month. Interest added, against payment taken.

41
00:03:06,470 --> 00:03:11,900
If the interest is bigger, you are renting the debt, not repaying it.

42
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:15,660
Three. Only then decide about overpaying.

43
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:26,350
Above the crossover it genuinely shortens it. Far below, and written off anyway, it is money burned. Same arithmetic, both directions.

44
00:03:26,350 --> 00:03:40,030
And for the ones coming behind you: qard hasan funds, employer tuition schemes, paying as you study. Smaller, slower, less convenient. Also not this.

45
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:45,450
You didn't fail to pay it off. You were never paying it off.

46
00:03:45,450 --> 00:03:46,938
The Money Machine, Decoded.
